<task id="125" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rebuild and redeploy the guest-auth fix to dev; guest + member live check</title>
    <phase>7 — B2B guest sign-in on Dataverse surfaces (#1453), owner 2026-10-08</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deployments of many PCFs/code pages to a shared environment.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Many deploys with ordering and verification.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <deps>122, 123, 124</deps>
    <tags>deploy, pcf, code-page, auth</tags>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>After 122-124 merge: rebuild every surface that bundles @spaarke/auth and deploy the affected ones to spaarkedev1. Each Dataverse deploy needs the owner's go (ask once with the full list).</prompt>
  <goal>All surfaces in `notes/122-guest-signin-review.md` "fail for a guest" are redeployed from master; the owner's guest and a member both open a matter and a document without a sign-in error.</goal>
  <constraints>
    <constraint>Owner go before any deploy; deploy from a fresh short-path worktree of origin/master; check for concurrent deploys of the same controls by other sessions first.</constraint>
    <constraint>Build @spaarke/auth first (PCFs consume its dist); PCFs with `npm run build:prod` through scripts/Invoke-PcfBuildProd.ps1 (judge from output); solution import per the pcf-deploy skill; code pages via their Deploy-*.ps1.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>List the surfaces, versions and deploy commands; get the owner's go.</step>
    <step>Build and deploy; verify each deployed version.</step>
    <step>Read-only checks: the SPA redirect URIs for the MSAL client(s) include the Dataverse origin; the test guest's systemuser exists, is enabled and licensed (no writes).</step>
    <step>Owner live check: guest and member open a matter and a document (preview, related documents, communications, tracking), Daily Briefing, Email page; no AADSTS error, no 401.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every listed surface deployed from a master SHA, version recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Owner confirms guest and member live checks.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <justification>
    <existing>Existing deploy scripts.</existing>
    <extension>n/a — deployment.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The fix never reaches users (the library is bundled into each surface).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
</task>
